FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with the FerrionOS patches before it in recipe.toml applied, ferrion-drm-page-flip.patch last among them. It joins the submissions of ferrion-gpu-submit.patch to the sync objects and sync files of ferrion-gpu-syncobj.patch:
- A submission's fence is a FenceLeaf that virtio-gpud signals when the device answers the fenced SUBMIT_3D, or signals with an error when the device refuses it. VIRTGPU_EXECBUF_FENCE_FD_OUT gives a sync file around it, so merge, file info and poll work on submission fences; the fence descriptor type of ferrion-gpu-submit.patch and its test-only unsignaled command are gone.
- Out sync objects get the submission's fence at their point (a binary sync object at point 0, a timeline at its point), after every one named has been checked; in sync objects and a VIRTGPU_EXECBUF_FENCE_FD_IN sync file are waited for before the submission reaches the device, the request staying blocked without blocking the driver, as Linux blocks the caller; VIRTGPU_EXECBUF_SYNCOBJ_RESET resets an in sync object after the submission. Unknown sync-object flags get EINVAL, an unknown sync object ENOENT, a binary sync object or point with no fence EINVAL, as in Linux.
- WAIT and the fences buffers keep are the same sync fences.

